  "summary": "The scene is built and typechecks. `aura3d render` produced no errors and a non-black frame with motion. The last screenshot shows the red car on the turntable with a faint mirrored copy below it. I did not look at the later frames, so the rotation rate and the angle readout were not checked against the screenshots.\n\n- **Object:** `recipes/showroom.mjs` builds a streamlined red body, a cabin bump with a black glass band over it, four rubber wheels with dark hubs and chrome rings, and chrome trim on the belt line and along the body's waist. It was imported with `import_three` as the `showroom` asset.\n- **Paint:** The paint has a glossy clear coat over a deep red base. The metallic flakes come from a random normal map that is baked into the model and tiled across the body.\n- **Turntable and mirror:** The platform is a dark glossy disc with a chrome lip and a cool ring light. The faint reflection is a flipped copy of the car under a semi-transparent floor. I turned the floor's reflectivity down, but the disc still reads silvery at the shallow viewing angle.\n- **Lighting and camera:** The environment is the engine's softbox studio preset on a dark background. On top of it are three long rect strip lights (one overhead, one each side), a faint cool rim light and a light bloom. The camera is fixed at a low front-three-quarter angle with the car in frame.\n- **Motion and state:** `src/main.ts` rotates the model at 20°/s each frame. It sets `window.__TASK_STATE__` to `{ turntableAngleDeg, paintFinish: 'clearcoat' }`, with the angle increasing every frame. `__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frame.\n\nThe cabin still looks a little like a separate dome rather than a blended shoulder, and the strip-light reflections on the body are subtle rather than long bands.\n\n"
